From d63d03916cc5a04579f2e994b45050cf6635a4c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:14:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] The separation of the 3D view is the person's depth
 limits and nothing else

The two cameras' separation is the largest under which the farthest and nearest displayed point stay inside the sunk and popped
limits the desktop gives the window (libstereo-declare 1.10, _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_DEPTH_LIMITS), read again while the window is
open; with none the two eyes are the same picture and the program says so in the ten languages. The physical parameters (screen
width and distance, eye separation, strength) are gone from StereoParams.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
